menu "Room hub: sensors"

    config HUB_PIR_FITTED
        bool "HC-SR501 presence sensor (PIR) fitted"
        default y
        help
            Off: the presence input is not read, published nor sent on CAN, and the
            rules built on presence (inactivity, night exit) are suspended. An
            unplugged PIR reads as "nobody here", which would raise a false
            inactivity alert by day.

    config HUB_LM35_FITTED
        bool "LM35 temperature sensor fitted"
        default y
        help
            Off: no temperature is read, published nor sent on CAN, and the
            temperature rule never fires. A fitted LM35 that comes loose is caught
            anyway: readings outside 0-57 degC are dropped, with one warning.

    config HUB_DOORS_ABSENT
        string "Doors not fitted (ids of BOARD_DOORS, comma separated)"
        default ""
        help
            For example "banheiro" or "quarto,banheiro". An unplugged reed switch
            reads as "open", which would raise false night exit alerts. A door
            listed here is not read, published nor sent on CAN, and the rules never
            see it move. The other doors keep their indexes and CAN ids.

endmenu
